      "group": "demo",
      "input": "   This AGREEMENT  is  a  sample  for  testing  the   electronic\r\n   translation program \"LTGOLD\".\r\n         \r\n         \r\n   AGREEMENT  #SA111111\r\n\r\n        AGREEMENT ON SUPPLY OF FISH MEAL\r\n\r\n        This AGREEMENT  ON  SUPPLY  OF  FISH  MEAL  (hereinafter\r\n   \"AGREEMENT\")  is  made  as  of the _______ day of __________,\r\n   1992,   in   St.   Petersburg,   Russia,   by   and   between\r\n   ____________________________________________________________\r\n   ____________________________________________________________\r\n   ____________________________________________________________\r\n   Represented  by  ____________________________________________\r\n   its _________________________ (hereinafter \"SELLER\"), and ABC\r\n   Company, 2000 South 10th Avenue, Lebanon, Oregon, 97355, USA,\r\n   An  American Corporation,  registered in the state of Oregon,\r\n   USA,  represented by  Bill DUMPTY,  its  Vice  President   of\r\n   Project  Development,  Russia  (hereinafter  \"SELLER\").  Both\r\n   BUYER and SELLER (hereinafter \"PARTIES\") agree to comply with\r\n   all  terms  and  conditions  defined  in this AGREEMENT.  The\r\n   PARTIES  to  this  AGREEMENT  acknowledge  they  are  legally\r\n   authorized   to   represent   their   organizations  and  all\r\n   negotiations were agreed to by each  Party  under  their  own\r\n   free will. This AGREEMENT is made in both Russian and English\r\n   with both languages having equal validity under law.\r\n\r\n        1.  PRODUCTS\r\n\r\n        SELLER  shall supply to  BUYER  1,000,000  (one  million)\r\n    Metric  tons  of  Fish Meal,  as defined in BUYER'S pro forma\r\n    Invoice #DMO122122, attached hereto and made an integral part\r\n    of this AGREEMENT as EXHIBIT \"A\" (hereinafter \"PRODUCTS\")\r\n\r\n        2. PRICE AND TOTAL VALUE\r\n\r\n        The total price for the goods and services as defined  in\r\n    EXHIBIT \"A\" is USD $____,______,_____ ( United States Dollars\r\n    and  no  cents) (hereinafter \"PRICE\").  The PRICE is firm and\r\n    not subject  to  any  modifications  for  the  term  of  this\r\n    AGREEMENT\r\n\r\n\r\n        3. DELIVERY TERMS\r\n\r\n        The delivery of the PRODUCTS shall be  upon  presentation\r\n    of all documents as defined in EXHIBIT \"A\".  The products and\r\n    services are delivered under international standards for  FOB\r\n    (Freight On Board) shipments.\r\n\r\n        4. TERMS OF PAYMENT\r\n\r\n        BUYER  shall  present  the  SELLER  with  an Irrevocable,\r\n    divisible,  transferable,  confirmed,  assignable in part  or\r\n    total  revolving  Letter of Credit issued by an international\r\n    bank.  The Letter of Credit shall allow for partial shipments\r\n    and partial payment. The Letter of Credit shall be subject to\r\n    the uniform custom and practices for documentary credit (1980\r\n    Revision) as defined in the International Chamber of Commerce\r\n    Publication no. 400. Payment of the Letter of credit shall be\r\n    made  upon  delivery  of  Documents for Payment as defined in\r\n    item 13-F of EXHIBIT \"A\". If the SELLER is unable to meet its\r\n    obligations  under  this AGREEMENT,  SELLER shall release all\r\n    remaining portion(s) of the Letter  of  Credit  back  to  the\r\n    BUYER  within  30  (thirty)  days  of  notifying BUYER of its\r\n    inability to do so.\r\n\r\n        5. WARRANTY\r\n\r\n        The  quality of  the  PRODUCTS  shall  conform  with  the\r\n    specifications  as  defined  in  EXHIBIT  \"A\".  The exclusive\r\n    remedy for breach of this warranty shall be the  replacement,\r\n    at  the  SELLERS  option,  damages  shall  be  limited to the\r\n    purchase price of the PRODUCTS involved.  IN NO  EVENT  SHALL\r\n    SELLER  BE  RESPONSIBLE FOR CONSEQUENTIAL OR SPECIAL DAMAGES.\r\n    THE FOREGOING WARRANTIES ARE IN LIEU OF ALL OTHER WARRANTIES,\r\n    EXPRESSED  OR  IMPLIED,  INCLUDING  THE  IMPLIED  WARRANTY OF\r\n    MERCHANTABILITY FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.\r\n\r\n        6. PACKING AND MARKING\r\n\r\n        Packing is  to ensure  full  safety  of  PRODUCTS  during\r\n    transportation   by   all   means   of   transport  including\r\n    transshipments. Each package shall have the following painted\r\n    on  two  sides  with  indelible  paint or ink in both Russian\r\n    and/or English:  HANDLE WITH CARE,  FLAMMABLE,  DO  NOT  OVER\r\n    STACK,  GROSS  WEIGHT,  NET WEIGHT,  FISH MEAL,  and CONTRACT\r\n    #DMO22121.  The product shall be  packaged  in  50Kg.  (fifty\r\n    kilogram)  New,  Polk Jute Lined Bags or as agreed to by both\r\n    Parties.  BUYER may supply other forms of packaging  required\r\n    to meet clients requirements, at their cost.\r\n\r\n        7. FORCE-MAJEURE\r\n\r\n        The  PARTIES  shall  be  free  from  the  partial or full\r\n    obligations under this AGREEMENT which results from any cause\r\n    or  circumstance  beyond  the control of either party such as\r\n    fire,  flood,  government  or  industrial   intervention   or\r\n    insurrection,  earthquakes,  weather, etc. In addition to the\r\n    above,  Industry Standard Force Majeure provisions  apply  to\r\n    this  AGREEMENT  for \"Fish Meal\" as governed as per the rules\r\n    of the International Chamber of Commerce (hereinafter  \"ICC\")\r\n    Paris,  France,  Rules and Regulations, and ICC terms of 1988\r\n    with Amendments,  and any dispute arising from this AGREEMENT\r\n    for \"Fish Meal\" shall be settled according to these rules and\r\n    the decision of the ICC shall be final  and  binding  on  the\r\n    PARTIES hereto. Arbitration, if necessary, shall be conducted\r\n    in the English and Russian languages. Each PARTY shall notify\r\n    the  other  of  any  circumstances  which are likely to delay\r\n    delivery of  any  responsibility  or  obligation  under  this\r\n    AGREEMENT.  In this case,  the fulfillment of the obligations\r\n    shall extend for the period that said  circumstances  are  in\r\n    effect.  A  certificate  issued by the Chamber of Commerce of\r\n    the  PARTIES  choice  shall  be  sufficient  proof  of   such\r\n    circumstances and their duration.\r\n\r\n        8. ARBITRATION\r\n\r\n        The  BUYER   reserves   the   right   to  claim  for  the\r\n    fulfillment of the AGREEMENT within 60 days from the date  of\r\n    delivery. All disputes and differences which may arise out of\r\n    or in conjunction with this AGREEMENT shall be settled as far\r\n    as possible by means of negotiations between the PARTIES.  If\r\n    the PARTIES are unable to  resolve  a  dispute,  the  dispute\r\n    shall  be  heard in the court of the plaintiffs country,  the\r\n    decision of above said court shall be  final  and  obligatory\r\n    for the PARTIES.\r\n\r\n        9. GENERAL PROVISIONS\r\n\r\n        All exhibits mentioned above in  AGREEMENT are considered\r\n    as integral parts thereof.  All amendments and addenda to the\r\n    AGREEMENT  are not valid unless made in writing and signed by\r\n    the  PARTIES.  This  AGREEMENT   supersedes   all   preceding\r\n    negotiations and correspondence, making them null and void.\r\n\r\n        10. OTHER CONDITIONS\r\n\r\n        SELLER  shall  supply  BUYER  with  a  2%  (two percent )\r\n    performance bond for the value of the  Letter  of  Credit  to\r\n    activate the Letter of Credit,  \"unrestricted\".  SELLER shall\r\n    advise BUYER of shipment schedules within 5 days  of  signing\r\n    this AGREEMENT. BUYER shall be responsible for the scheduling\r\n    receipt of goods in the port  of  destination.  Both  PARTIES\r\n    shall  make  best  efforts  to  assure  that  both  schedules\r\n    coincide with each other.\r\n\r\n\r\n        11. EXCHANGE RATE\r\n\r\n        All payments  agreed  to by the parties shall be made  in\r\n    Russian Rubles or its successor, but protected by an exchange\r\n    rate  of  ______ ( ) Rubles per one USD$.  The fluctuation of\r\n    the Russian currency  shall  be  protected  by  the  Official\r\n    Exchange rate at the time of payment. An example of the above\r\n    protection is if at the time of signing  this  agreement  the\r\n    price per item is R3000 each,  and the official exchange rate\r\n    is R300 per 1 USD$ and the official exchange rate changes  to\r\n    R600  per  1  USD$ at the time of payment the BUYER shall pay\r\n    the SELLER R6000 per unit.  If  the  official  exchange  rate\r\n    falls  below  the rate at the signing of this agreement,  the\r\n    SELLER shall receive payment at the official exchange rate at\r\n    the signing of this agreement.\r\n\r\n\r\n        12. LEGAL ADDRESS OF THE PARTIES\r\n\r\n        The SELLER:\r\n         \r\n\r\n        The BUYER:\r\n\r\n",
